","id":171885206,"node_id":"U_kgDOCj7Clg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171885206?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK","html_url":"https://github.com/PateevK","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-30T07:08:11Z","updated_at":"2026-08-30T07:08:11Z","body":"> @PateevK Did you use AI?\r\n\r\n@DaveTheEggman . I did use AI to review my code changes before submiting PR. \r\nEverything else was done the normal-people-way\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5467308010/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5470844566","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122994#issuecomment-5470844566","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122994","id":5470844566,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRhZ2lg","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-30T19:41:13Z","updated_at":"2026-08-30T19:41:13Z","body":"I think we need a solution that works for Vulkan too. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5470844566/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5475738760","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122994#issuecomment-5475738760","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122994","id":5475738760,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRmEkiA","user":{"login":"PateevK","id":171885206,"node_id":"U_kgDOCj7Clg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171885206?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK","html_url":"https://github.com/PateevK","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-31T08:23:09Z","updated_at":"2026-08-31T10:07:12Z","body":"> I think we need a solution that works for Vulkan too.\r\n\r\nGLSL \"discard\" gets compiled into spirv \"OpKill\" that has to be guarded by a branch since there is no conditional OpKillif like dx.op.discard_if. \r\n\r\nI guess that intel DirectX drivers just dont expect dxil pattern like before `nir_peephole_opt` causing gpu hangs. \r\nWhile Vulkan intel drivers expect such spv pattern cause there is no other way to kill an execution.\r\n\r\nIf we were really to make control flow more uniform for Vulkan as well that would require VK_EXT_shader_demote_to_helper_invocation and change \"discard\" to \"demote\" in shaders.  \r\n\r\nAnyway taking that #118719 is only d3d12 issue,  i think intel vulkan drivers handle that spv pattern well.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5475738760/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5477909512","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122994#issuecomment-5477909512","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122994","id":5477909512,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRoJECA","user":{"login":"blueskythlikesclouds","id":19259897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjU5ODk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19259897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds","html_url":"https://github.com/blueskythlikesclouds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-31T11:52:39Z","updated_at":"2026-08-31T11:53:10Z","body":"This won't work with shader baking since the vendor at bake time may be different than the vendor at runtime. If the optimization doesn't hurt the conversion times, it could be included globally for all vendors.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5477909512/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5478246930","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122994#issuecomment-5478246930","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122994","id":5478246930,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRodqEg","user":{"login":"PateevK","id":171885206,"node_id":"U_kgDOCj7Clg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171885206?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK","html_url":"https://github.com/PateevK","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-31T12:19:56Z","updated_at":"2026-08-31T12:19:56Z","body":"> This won't work with shader baking since the vendor at bake time may be different than the vendor at runtime. If the optimization doesn't hurt the conversion times, it could be included globally for all vendors.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/5ec4857b340b6284a18b49b2eda462bd250f219a/drivers/d3d12/rendering_shader_container_d3d12.cpp#L387\r\n\r\n`dxil_spirv_nir_passes` already does a bunch of optimization passes. Adding a single additional pass shouldnt hurt the conversion times more then the margin of error. \r\n\r\nthe code itself is very simple, you can take a look:\r\n https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/blob/main/src/compiler/nir/nir_opt_peephole_select.c\r\n \r\n I could profile the code and measure difference (if there is any). \r\n What profiling instrumentation do you have in the code base ?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5478246930/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5479115503","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122994#issuecomment-5479115503","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122994","id":5479115503,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRpSq7w","user":{"login":"blueskythlikesclouds","id":19259897,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MjU5ODk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19259897?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds","html_url":"https://github.com/blueskythlikesclouds","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blueskythlikesclouds/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-31T13:32:38Z","updated_at":"2026-08-31T13:33:01Z","body":"> dxil_spirv_nir_passes already does a bunch of optimization passes. Adding a single additional pass shouldnt hurt the conversion times more then the margin of error.\r\n\r\nThese are disabled in Godot. It saved quite a significant amount of time to disable them without somehow much difference on the DXIL output.\r\n\r\nFor profiling I don't specifically use anything from Godot. I use Superluminal on Windows.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5479115503/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5480551448","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122994#issuecomment-5480551448","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122994","id":5480551448,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRqqUGA","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-31T15:28:12Z","updated_at":"2026-08-31T15:31:51Z","body":"> I could profile the code and measure difference (if there is any). What profiling instrumentation do you have in the code base ?\r\n\r\nWe have built in support for [Tracy](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine_details/development/profiling/tracy.html#tracy) and [Perfetto](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine_details/development/profiling/perfetto.html) \r\n\r\nThat being said, adding an optimization pass so that the compiler outputs slightly different code that just happens to workaround a driver bug is not the correct approach\r\n\r\nThe full text of the workaround is:\r\n\r\n> Issue: One EU executes while loop sequence, other EU breaks out. However, due to NoMask after endif, both EUs end up executing mov and send. JEU Fused Mask not correct in HW. WA: Disable Structured Control Flow by setting EnableVISAStructurizer.\r\n\r\nIt seems that using a select op instead of a branch works around the problem for now. But its not clear why the NoMask op is being emitted by the compiler. So I'm not convinced that this solution won't stop working in the future","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5480551448/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5481599572","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122994#issuecomment-5481599572","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122994","id":5481599572,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRrqSVA","user":{"login":"PateevK","id":171885206,"node_id":"U_kgDOCj7Clg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171885206?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK","html_url":"https://github.com/PateevK","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-31T16:55:11Z","updated_at":"2026-08-31T16:55:11Z","body":"> We have built in support for [Tracy](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine_details/development/profiling/tracy.html#tracy) and [Perfetto](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine_details/development/profiling/perfetto.html)\r\n\r\nThanks !\r\n\r\n> its not clear why the NoMask op is being emitted by the compiler\r\n\r\nye, its just how the intel d3d12 driver works and our hands are tied there. \r\nAll we can do is make control flow more unified so the issue is unlikely to be triggered.\r\nAnd thats exactly where the peephole opt comes at rescue.\r\n\r\n> adding an optimization pass so that the compiler outputs slightly different code that just happens to workaround a driver bug is not the correct approach\r\n\r\nIts debatable. \r\nAdding a low cost pass producing more predictable DXIL that is unlikely to trigger the driver issue can be a correct approach.\r\nIf anyone will come up with a better one I would be happy (￣▽￣)ノ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5481599572/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5497335797","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122994#issuecomment-5497335797","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122994","id":5497335797,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABR6qv9Q","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-01T16:47:26Z","updated_at":"2026-09-01T16:47:26Z","body":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120857 Seems to be related too","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5497335797/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5506917688","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122994#issuecomment-5506917688","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122994","id":5506917688,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSDzlOA","user":{"login":"PateevK","id":171885206,"node_id":"U_kgDOCj7Clg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171885206?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK","html_url":"https://github.com/PateevK","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-02T08:44:45Z","updated_at":"2026-09-02T08:44:45Z","body":"> #120857 Seems to be related too\r\n\r\nye, i was able to reproduce #120857, did a quick test. This PR fixed the issue as well.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5506917688/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5551775927","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122994#issuecomment-5551775927","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122994","id":5551775927,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSulgtw","user":{"login":"PateevK","id":171885206,"node_id":"U_kgDOCj7Clg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171885206?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK","html_url":"https://github.com/PateevK","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-05T12:20:47Z","updated_at":"2026-09-05T12:20:47Z","body":"i5-13450HX\r\n\r\nthe opt takes 30ms out of total 11s `_set_code_from_spirv`\r\n\r\nIf you eventually consider merging this, let me know, I'll remove Intel workaround code and enable it globally.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1819\" height=\"415\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1298472a-d006-46eb-af67-f1b3876cbd45\" />","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5551775927/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5703545368","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122994#issuecomment-5703545368","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122994","id":5703545368,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABU_UyGA","user":{"login":"Wagnard","id":11493785,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNDkzNzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11493785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard","html_url":"https://github.com/Wagnard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Wagnard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-16T19:46:58Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T19:46:58Z","body":"Tested this PR on an Arc B580 (Xe2, driver 32.0.101.8993) with the project from #120857, D3D12, shader cache cleared.\r\n\r\nBefore: device lost with DXGI_ERROR_DEVICE_HUNG (from GetDeviceRemovedReason(), which Godot doesn't call today — I added it locally). It was first observed in fence_wait, before any CreateGraphicsPipelineState, so the PSO errors in my earlier logs were a consequence, not the cause.\r\n\r\nAfter: no crash on the same scenario (dropped item behind the camera, then turn to face it — the most reliable trigger I have).\r\n\r\nNote that B580 is Xe2, which has no fused EUs, so this is outside the Intel workaround quoted above. The peephole pass still fixes it.\r\n\r\nTwo things I noticed in the diff: `nir_opt_peephole_select_options opts;` is not initialized (`limit` is undefined), and the shader cache key doesn't include the vendor, so applying the pass unconditionally seems safer than gating it on Intel.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5703545368/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5704249521","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122994#issuecomment-5704249521","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122994","id":5704249521,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABU__wsQ","user":{"login":"PateevK","id":171885206,"node_id":"U_kgDOCj7Clg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/171885206?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK","html_url":"https://github.com/PateevK","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PateevK/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-16T20:44:35Z","updated_at":"2026-09-16T20:44:35Z","body":"@Wagnard thanks for the catch with not zero initialized options.\r\n\r\nI've removed driver workaround condition and fixed the init.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5704249521/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]